{"answer":"No. A duration close to your usual does not mean you are sleeping well when you are repeatedly waking and feel exhausted afterward. Your report matters, and a consumer device cannot verify restorative sleep or dismiss those symptoms. [1703636d-context] [1703636d-e19]

The recent record also includes some worse-than-normal sleep and fatigue reports, although the latest logged reports were normal; it cannot capture the repeated awakenings you describe today. [1703636d-e3]

When did this start, and what changed around then? Do you have any current pain? Also, is there any recent exercise or physical work not captured in the log?","outcome":"clarification","reason":"The device record cannot establish sleep quality or explain the newly reported exhaustion; clarification is needed about timing, pain, and unrecorded load."}

